All four plugin skill trees — Claude, Codex, OpenCode, and Antigravity — are rendered from the shared template tree skills-src/git-span by scripts/build-agent-skills.mjs, so the expert, triage, whole-file-anchor, and reconcile guidance and the core skill's never-narrow gotcha bullet land identically on every tree from a single template edit. Deliberately per-platform — expressed as it.variant branches in the anchored templates, never hand edits to the rendered trees — are the harness dispatch/vocabulary sections: the reconcile team spawn syntax (team.md's Antigravity branch dispatches by prose, having no pinned subagent tool name), understanding-hook-output's channel semantics, the core skill's hook-vocabulary items (the Same-commit workflow event names and the Where-to-go-next install pointer), hookignore's event names, the cleanup campaign's worker dispatch, and the candidate finder's installed-skill script paths — plus the install flow in install-and-trust.md, whose per-platform bodies describe the Codex marketplace/trust flow, the OpenCode npm plugin array and npx installer, and the Antigravity agy plugin install into ~/.gemini/config/plugins. The expert is the one surface still forked by hand: agents/expert.md lives outside skills-src on the Claude, Codex, and OpenCode trees only — Antigravity ships no expert agent. A standing vitest control (packages/agent-hooks test/opencode/skill-tree-vocabulary.test.ts) greps the opencode skill tree for twin-only vocabulary outside these sanctioned spots.
